stateDiagram-v2
    direction LR
    state "no user row" as no_user
    state "is_email_verified = false" as unverified
    state "token unused + valid" as token_valid
    state "token unused + expired" as token_expired
    state "token used" as token_used
    state "is_email_verified = true" as verified

    [*] --> no_user
    no_user --> unverified: POST register [unique email and phone] / hash password and create member
    unverified --> token_valid: register transaction / store hashed token and expiry
    token_valid --> verified: GET verify-email [hash found, unused, not expired] / set verified timestamp and used_at
    token_valid --> token_expired: time passes [expires_at < now] / verification rejected
    token_used --> verified: repeated verification / return already verified
    verified --> [*]: login [password valid] / issue access token
    unverified --> unverified: login / reject EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED
    no_user --> verified: verified OAuth or staff provisioning / create verified user directly

    note bottom of token_valid
        Only the token hash is stored. Verification lookup does not lock the token row.
        Registration remains committed if email delivery fails.
    end note
    note bottom of token_expired
        No resend-verification endpoint is implemented.
    end note
